# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Docs (Sphinx / Read the Docs build output)
/docs/_build/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.whl
*.so
*.dylib
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Generated graphs / scan artifacts (never committed — rebuilt from fixtures)
*.kgl
/scan-out/

# Audio — NEVER committed (copyright + size). The gate's fixtures are frozen
# TrackAnalysis records; the real music library is maintainer-machine-only.
*.mp3
*.flac
*.wav
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.aac

# Secrets / Environment
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.secret
credentials.json
secrets.toml

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.settings/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Agent skills (local only). `.agents/skills/` holds the skills and
# `.claude/skills` is a symlink to it; `AGENTS.md`, the instructions file, is
# tracked.
.claude/
/.agents/

# Local dev working folder + cross-project coordination channel — never
# committed. Each has a README describing its own layout, and the
# dev-docs-cleanup / read-inbox skills own the auto-purged tiers within.
# No tracked code may cite a path inside either: the citation would outlive the
# file it names and become a dangling instruction. `AGENTS.md` is the
# exception: it is the agents' map of these folders.
/dev-docs/
/inbox/

# Coverage / profiling
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info
htmlcov/
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
